57bm-i1a"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i1a"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i1a","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.89 (The next floor quotient)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.89, p. 70, label record:257bm-i1a","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For $d\\ge2$ and $M\\ge0$, the floor quotient satisfies\n$$\nq(M+1,d)=2q(M,d)+\\mathbf1_{d\\mid M+1}.\n$$\nIndeed, $q(M,d)=\\sum_{j=1}^{\\lfloor M/d\\rfloor}2^{M-jd}$. Increasing $M$ doubles each existing term and adds $1$ exactly when $M+1$ is divisible by $d$. Thus a quotient doubles or doubles plus one; it does not remain unchanged except when both values are zero. Summing over a fixed finite support gives the corresponding update with added term $c_D(M+1)$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i1a","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i1a","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i1a%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_floor_quotient_geometric_sum%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i1a%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_floor_quotient_geometric_sum%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_floor_quotient_geometric_sum"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i1a","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i1a%22%2C%22lean